I played NetHack on-and-off for almost ten years unspoiled.  I never really
came close to ascending, but I did make it past the castle a few times.
(Now that I'm spoiled, of course, getting to the castle almost guarantees
ascension.)

The reason (IMO) people on NAO seem to have so many problems is that their
first recourse is generally to ask for help when they get into a bad
situation rather than "experiment, probably die, and learn from it", or
even "carefully look through long lists of spoilers and attempt to
formulate the best plan of action".  Asking experienced players for help is
much faster on the IRC channel, and if the resource is so convenient and
easy it's hard not to use it.

I believe that, given strong enough motivation, I could have *eventually*
ascended unspoiled, but that it would have been a matter of years or
possibly decades rather than weeks or months.  However, I'm more interested
in the strategy of NetHack than in the long arduous process of discovery.
There are some things I'm sure I would *never* have figured out, such as
magic cancellation.

